   "title": "Rain or snow in the US Northeast? The snow line climbs to 11,811 ft at Cannon Mountain (21 November)",
   "description": "The forecast keeps the 0 °C level in the US Northeast between 0 ft (0 m) and 12,861 ft (3,920 m) for the next days. The snow line, about 984 ft …",
   "lede": "The forecast keeps the 0 °C level in the US Northeast between 0 ft (0 m) and 12,861 ft (3,920 m) for the next days. The snow line, about 984 ft (300 m) lower, peaks at 11,811 ft (3,600 m) at Cannon Mountain on Saturday 21 November. Confidence: good for the trend, lower for any single number.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "The 0 °C level, daily",
     "p": [
      "The 0 °C level at the resorts below, from the coldest to the warmest hour of each day: Saturday 21 November: from 11,089 ft (3,380 m) to 12,861 ft (3,920 m). Sunday 22 November: from 7,251 ft (2,210 m) to 12,861 ft (3,920 m). Monday 23 November: from 164 ft (50 m) to 11,516 ft (3,510 m). Tuesday 24 November: from 0 ft (0 m) to 656 ft (200 m)."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Snow line by resort",
     "p": [
      "Whiteface Mountain, base 1,220 ft (372 m), top 4,373 ft (1,333 m): snow line near 11,483 ft (3,500 m) on 21 November, over the top of the lifts; rain or wet snow everywhere if anything falls.",
      "Cannon Mountain (base 1,883 ft (574 m), top 4,039 ft (1,231 m)): snow line about 11,811 ft (3,600 m) on 21 November, above the top. The whole mountain is in the rain-or-wet-snow zone if precipitation falls.",
      "Smugglers' Notch Resort, base 1,115 ft (340 m), top 3,648 ft (1,112 m): snow line near 11,811 ft (3,600 m) on 21 November, over the top of the lifts; rain or wet snow everywhere if anything falls.",
      "Bolton Valley Resort (base 1,558 ft (475 m), top 3,117 ft (950 m)): snow line about 10,499 ft (3,200 m) on 21 November, above the top. The whole mountain is in the rain-or-wet-snow zone if precipitation falls.",
      "Middlebury College Snow Bowl, base 1,709 ft (521 m), top 2,661 ft (811 m): snow line near 11,483 ft (3,500 m) on 21 November, over the top of the lifts; rain or wet snow everywhere if anything falls."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Rain-on-snow risk",
     "p": [
      "Rain-on-snow risk in the next days: none that we can see. The snow line stays low enough on the wet days.",
      "Tug Hill (1,706 ft (520 m)): 6 mm forecast, snow line near 1,542 ft (470 m) while it falls.",
      "The forecast gives Stowe (4,393 ft (1,339 m)) 16 mm of precipitation, with the snow line near 3,806 ft (1,160 m) during the wet hours."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "The 0 °C level and the snow line, briefly",
     "p": [
      "Air cools with height, as a rule. Below the 0 °C level flakes begin to melt; melting is slow, so rain starts only some 984 ft (300 m) lower. That is the snow line. Dry air cools the snow by evaporation and pushes the line lower still."
     ]
    }
   ],
